/-!
# The representation-classification reduction for H.4.7

For a faithful finite-dimensional binary action with F*(M) genuinely
isomorphic to PSL₃(4) and irreducible on the space, the concrete SL₃ catalogue
reduces to five nontrivial central-quotient words. Their exact Schur degrees
give binary dimensions 9, 16 and 64. The dimension-nine alternatives retain
actual equivalences over the algebraic closure of the commuting field.

The equality predicates specify the actual descended Hermitian tensor or its
dual and a genuine field automorphism of the component. The non-tensor cubic
spectrum, inversion of a cubic by an ambient involution, and descent of the
two natural words to those Hermitian models remain necessary before the full
involution bound and equality characterization can be assembled here.

Source: Aschbacher–Smith H.4.7, printed pp.382–383 of refs/quasithin.pdf.
The application in Chapter 5 is on printed p.641. This module currently
exports the proved classification reduction, not a theorem named H.4.7.
-/
